test/check/error-primes.sumspec:6:36:
  |
6 | Page = Home | Plan (A * B) | Many [B]
  |                                    ^
warning: a list goes only as a whole type definition; give it a type name, such as Points = [Point], and write the name here (an error from SumSpec 1.2)

test/check/error-primes.sumspec:8:18:
  |
8 | onSource :: App(A') -> App(A)
  |                  ^
a prime (') marks a new value, so it can only be on the target side

test/check/error-primes.sumspec:9:23:
  |
9 | twice :: App -> App(A'')
  |                       ^
a name takes at most one prime (')

test/check/error-primes.sumspec:10:33:
   |
10 | onPath :: Page.Home -> Page.Plan'
   |                                 ^
a prime (') goes only on a bare type name; a written variant or argument already says what the new value is

test/check/error-primes.sumspec:11:40:
   |
11 | onArgs :: Page.Home -> Page.Plan(A * B)'
   |                                        ^
a prime (') goes only on a bare type name; a written variant or argument already says what the new value is

test/check/error-primes.sumspec:12:35:
   |
12 | onList :: Page.Home -> Page.Many([B]')
   |                                   ^
warning: a list isn't written in a pattern; give it a type name, such as Ids = [Id], and write the name (Ids, or Ids#ids to name it) (an error from SumSpec 1.2)

test/check/error-primes.sumspec:12:37:
   |
12 | onList :: Page.Home -> Page.Many([B]')
   |                                     ^
a prime (') goes only on a bare type name; a written variant or argument already says what the new value is

